cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ProteinViz, please cite it as below, together with the data resources it uses."
title: "ProteinViz: a provenance-first explorer for disease pathways, protein interactions and structures"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmed
    given-names: Shekib
    # orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000  # add your ORCID iD
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/shekibahmed/ProteinViz"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - protein-protein interaction
  - disease pathways
  - structural biology
  - AlphaFold
  - Open Targets
  - STRING
abstract: >-
  ProteinViz chains public resources (Open Targets, STRING, UniProt, RCSB PDB,
  AlphaFold DB and ChEMBL) into one workflow from a disease to its associated
  targets, enriched pathways, interaction networks, 3D structures with
  coordinate-derived interface residues, and compound activities, with
  provenance recorded for every result.
